விறலி","gloss":"female dancers"}],"gloss":"female dancers"},{"surface":"முன்கையும்","parts":[{"text":"முன்கை","lemma":"முன்கை","gloss":"forearm"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"also"}],"gloss":"forearm also"},{"surface":"தொடியின்","parts":[{"text":"தொடி","lemma":"தொடி","gloss":"bangle"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"with"}],"gloss":"with bangles"},{"surface":"பொலியா","parts":[{"text":"பொலியா","lemma":"பொலி","gloss":"do not shine"}],"gloss":"do not shine"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"இரவல்","parts":[{"text":"இரவல்","lemma":"இரவல்","gloss":"begging"}],"gloss":"begging"},{"surface":"மாக்களும்","parts":[{"text":"மாக்கள்","lemma":"மாக்கள்","gloss":"people"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"also"}],"gloss":"people also"},{"surface":"…","parts":[{"text":"…","lemma":"…","gloss":"…"}],"gloss":"…"}]}],"literal":"The song also indeed is obtained damaged / The heads of bards also, bees having gone, do not hum upon / The forearms of female dancers also do not shine with bangles / The begging people also …","translation":"The song itself is preserved only in a damaged state. Bees no longer swarm and hum over the heads of the bards, the forearms of the dancing women no longer shine with bangles, and the needy people who beg...","modern":"இப்பாடலும் சிதைந்த நிலையிலேயே கிடைத்துள்ளது. பாணர்களுடைய தலையிலே வண்டுகள் சென்று மொய்ப்பதில்லை; விறலியரின் முன்கைகள் வளையல்களால் பொலிவு பெறுவதில்லை; இரவலர்களாகிய மக்களும்...","explanation":"This is a fragmented Puram poem belonging to the theme of mourning (Kanchi tinai), lamenting the death of a generous patron. The first line is a modern editorial note indicating that the manuscript of the poem was found in a damaged state. The remaining lines describe the sorrowful state of the court after the patron's demise. Since the patron is gone, the bards (pāṇar) no longer wear the fresh, fragrant flower wreaths he used to give them, so bees do not swarm around their heads. The female dancers (viṟaliyar) no longer wear the golden bangles (toṭi) he gifted, leaving their forearms bare and without luster. The poem cuts off while describing the plight of the begging mendicants (iraval makkaḷ) who have lost their sole protector.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,1.1],[1.1,1.7],[1.7,2.6],[2.6,2.9],[2.9,3.6],[3.6,3.9],[3.9,4.58],[4.72,5.4],[5.4,5.53],[5.53,5.53],[5.53,5.53],[5.53,5.6]],"female":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,1.2],[1.2,1.9],[1.9,2.7],[2.7,3.1],[3.1,3.9],[3.9,4.2],[4.2,5.4],[5.4,6.24],[6.24,6.36],[6.36,6.36],[6.36,6.6],[6.6,8.3]]}}